---
import ProjectLayout from "../../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="1080 Sim"
  category="Project | Modular Motion Simulator"
  year="2026"
  description="Modular low-cost motion simulator concept for flight and driving simulation, designed to maximise immersion while reducing system complexity and cost."
>

  <p slot="intro">
    A modular motion simulator concept designed for both flight and driving,
    combining immersive motion cues, adaptable ergonomics and reduced mechanical cost.
  </p>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      01
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Objective
      </h2>

      <p>
        1080 Sim is a motion simulator concept designed to provide a high level
        of immersion for flight and driving simulation while keeping the mechanical
        architecture significantly simpler and more affordable than conventional
        full-motion platforms.
      </p>

      <p>
        The objective is not to reproduce every vehicle motion at full scale,
        but to generate the most perceptually relevant motion cues with a compact,
        efficient and adaptable system.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      02
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        One platform, multiple uses
      </h2>

      <p>
        The simulator is intended to support different simulation environments
        without requiring a dedicated platform for each application.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Flight simulation
        </li>

        <li>
          Racing simulation
        </li>

        <li>
          Road vehicle simulation
        </li>

        <li>
          Training and virtual testing
        </li>

        <li>
          Entertainment and immersive applications
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        The same motion architecture can therefore be reused with different seats,
        controls, software profiles and cockpit configurations.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      03
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Lower-cost architecture
      </h2>

      <p>
        Traditional motion simulators can require large structures, several
        high-power actuators and expensive precision components.
      </p>

      <p>
        1080 Sim explores a more economical architecture by reducing the moving mass,
        simplifying the mechanical transmission and concentrating motion where it has
        the greatest effect on the user's perception.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Reduced moving mass
        </li>

        <li>
          Fewer high-cost components
        </li>

        <li>
          Smaller actuator requirements
        </li>

        <li>
          Reduced structural footprint
        </li>

        <li>
          Lower installation complexity
        </li>
      </ul>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      04
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Perceived motion
      </h2>

      <p>
        A simulator does not necessarily need to reproduce the full displacement
        of a real vehicle to create a convincing sensation of motion.
      </p>

      <p>
        By controlling acceleration, rotation and short dynamic movements around
        the user, the system can reproduce key motion cues associated with braking,
        acceleration, cornering, turbulence, pitch and roll.
      </p>

      <p>
        This approach makes it possible to achieve strong immersion with a much
        smaller mechanical travel.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      05
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Modular cockpit
      </h2>

      <p>
        The simulator is designed around a modular cockpit architecture.
      </p>

      <p>
        Steering wheels, pedals, flight controls, seats and additional interfaces
        can be changed depending on the selected simulation mode.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Interchangeable driving controls
        </li>

        <li>
          Flight stick and throttle integration
        </li>

        <li>
          Adjustable seating position
        </li>

        <li>
          Adaptable display or VR configuration
        </li>

        <li>
          Modular peripheral mounting
        </li>
      </ul>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      06
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Compact design
      </h2>

      <p>
        One of the main advantages of the concept is the possibility of reducing
        the overall dimensions compared with traditional large motion platforms.
      </p>

      <p>
        A compact architecture makes the system easier to transport, install and
        integrate into domestic, educational or professional environments.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      07
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Energy efficiency
      </h2>

      <p>
        Reducing the mass that must be accelerated directly reduces the mechanical
        effort required from the actuators.
      </p>

      <p>
        This can make it possible to use smaller actuators, reduce energy consumption
        and lower the structural loads transmitted through the simulator frame.
      </p>

      <p>
        The result is a system that can remain highly dynamic without requiring
        the power levels associated with heavier motion platforms.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      08
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Software adaptability
      </h2>

      <p>
        The same mechanical platform can be controlled using different motion profiles
        depending on the simulation environment.
      </p>

      <p>
        Vehicle telemetry can be converted into motion commands adapted to the available
        travel and actuator dynamics.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Acceleration and braking cues
        </li>

        <li>
          Cornering forces
        </li>

        <li>
          Pitch and roll
        </li>

        <li>
          Turbulence
        </li>

        <li>
          Road or terrain feedback
        </li>
      </ul>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      09
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Advantages
      </h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          Lower mechanical cost than conventional full-motion simulators
        </li>

        <li>
          Reduced moving mass
        </li>

        <li>
          Lower actuator power requirements
        </li>

        <li>
          Compact footprint
        </li>

        <li>
          Modular flight and driving configurations
        </li>

        <li>
          Easier maintenance
        </li>

        <li>
          Lower energy consumption
        </li>

        <li>
          Adaptable motion profiles
        </li>

        <li>
          Compatibility with VR and conventional displays
        </li>
      </ul>

    </div>

  </section>


  <section class="detail-section">

    <div class="detail-index">
      10
    </div>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Vision
      </h2>

      <p>
        1080 Sim explores how motion simulation can become more accessible without
        sacrificing the key sensations responsible for immersion.
      </p>

      <p>
        By focusing on perceptually useful movements rather than maximum mechanical
        travel, the concept aims to provide a more compact, efficient and affordable
        alternative to traditional motion platforms.
      </p>

      <p>
        The long-term objective is to create a single adaptable system capable of
        supporting both flight and vehicle simulation with a high degree of realism.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>

</ProjectLayout>